Thread

A thread exists inside a process.

Example:

Chrome Process

Chrome
   |
   |-- Thread 1
   |-- Thread 2
   |-- Thread 3
Visualization

Without Threads:

Chrome Process
      |
      |
 One Execution Path

With Threads:

Chrome Process
      |
 ----------------
 |      |      |
 T1     T2     T3

Multiple execution paths.

What Does a Thread Have?

Each thread has its own:

Program Counter (PC)
Registers
Stack

But shares:

Code
Data
Files
Memory

with other threads in the same process.

Why Share Resources?

Because creating a new process is expensive.

Creating a thread is cheaper.

Example:

Instead of:

Chrome Process A
Chrome Process B
Chrome Process C

Use:

Chrome Process
